[2026-05-22 14:38]

PO call on #35 architectural fork: **Option B — ship CSR as-is, defer SSR + mock harness to follow-up CHORE.**

CHORE filed as **GH #36** (E2E Entu mock harness + flip landing page to SSR consumption).

### Your action

Mark the failing SSR-presence test as `.skip()` in `tests/frontend-scaffolding.spec.ts`:

```ts
test.skip('signed-in: page data is SSR-present in initial HTML (no flash-of-empty)', async ({ page }) => {
  // SKIP: pending CHORE-36 (Entu mock harness) — Playwright cannot intercept SvelteKit's
  // internal event.fetch, so SSR cannot be tested today without upstream-Entu mocking.
  // Un-skip when CHORE-36 lands.
  ...existing test body...
});
```

(Or `test('...', { skip: 'pending CHORE-36' }, ...)` if your Playwright version supports the metadata form — your call which reads cleaner.)

Also bundle this into the same commit as your pending import-path + cast fixes if you haven't pushed those yet. If you've already pushed those, this is a separate small commit.

Commit message convention: `test(#35): skip SSR-presence test pending CHORE-36 (mock harness)`. Branch is still `feat/bff-... wait — feat/frontend-scaffolding-mvp`. `git branch --show-current` before commit.

No need to message back. Just push.

### Authoring convention note (going forward, not for #35)

All new BFF-consuming pages should be authored against `data.*` SSR consumption (read from `$props()`), not `$effect`-fetch. SSR-presence E2E tests get `.skip()` with `// SKIP: pending CHORE-36`. Flip-day refactor then only touches existing CSR-drift, not every new page. This convention is logged in CHORE-36's body.
